From 9ffb76aee9e7753ae33909ba8441d75e8813dc05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:38:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] Reword the toolbar shortcut window width note

The description on the New tab and Add to bookmarks options read "Only available
for small windows", which reads as a restriction that excludes phones. It means
the opposite: a phone is a small window, so those shortcuts do work, and they are
hidden on tablets and wide desktop windows where the same actions already appear
in the tab strip or omnibox.

Now reads "Hidden when the browser window is wide", which describes the same rule
without implying the shortcut is unavailable on the device most people run this
on.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/android/strings/android_chrome_strings.grd | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/android/strings/android_chrome_strings.grd b/chrome/browser/ui/android/strings/android_chrome_strings.grd
index 21d88260be..fa8fe01efb 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/android/strings/android_chrome_strings.grd
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/android/strings/android_chrome_strings.grd
@@ -4114,7 +4114,7 @@ To change this setting, <ph name="BEGIN_LINK">BEGIN_LINK</ph>delete the Chrome d
         Current recommendation:  <ph name="RECOMMENDATION">%1$s<ex>New tab</ex></ph>
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_ADAPTIVE_TOOLBAR_BUTTON_PREFERENCE_BASED_ON_WINDOW_WIDTH_DESCRIPTION" desc="Description for based window width option.">
-        Only available for small windows
+        Hidden when the browser window is wide
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_TOOLBAR_SHORTCUT" desc="Title for toolbar shortcut toggle button in adaptive toolbar button preference page.">
         Toolbar shortcut
